       if not isinstance(pred_tokens, int) or pred_tokens <= 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"prediction_tokens must be positive integer\")\n        if not isinstance(parseable, bool):\n            raise ValueError(\"parseable must be boolean\")\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\n        normalized_gain = gain / pred_tokens\n        # round to 6 decimals\n        normalized_gain_rounded = round(normalized_gain, 6)\n        accepted = parseable and normalized_gain >= threshold\n        diagnostics.append({\n            \"accepted\": accepted,\n            \"call_id\": call_id,\n            \"normalized_gain\": normalized_gain_rounded\n        })\n        if accepted:\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\n    return {\n        \"accepted_call_ids\": accepted_call_ids,\n        \"diagnostics\": diagnostics\n    }\n\nBut note: The condition uses normalized_gain >= threshold, not the rounded one. Should we compare rounded or exact? Since threshold is given as 0.05, and normalized_gain might be just above due to rounding. The problem says \"normalized gain at or above threshold\". We'll use the exact computed normalized_gain (before rounding) for the comparison, but output the rounded value. That seems correct.\n\nNow we need to format the code as a string, escaping for JSON.\n\nWe'll output: {\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n ...\"} with proper escaping.\n\nWe must not use any imports except standard library, but we don't need any.\n\nNow produce final answer."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":2164,"completion_tokens":2484,"total_tokens":4648,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":2048},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":1883},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":2048,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":116},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}